 "title": "The entangled bank",
 "brief": "A dense, rounded thicket of small seeds, far more than the space can hold, packed into a loose sphere and trembling as they crowd each other: every species produces more young than can survive. Through the thicket run a few long, slow tendrils in two of the theme's green and teal hues, the branching paths of descent that Darwin draws in his one figure.\n\nA warm light, the season, wanders slowly through the scene. Seven larger buds sit at the edge of the thicket, and each one swells when the light comes near and shrinks back when it moves away: fitness is not a property of the bud alone but of where conditions happen to fall. Seeds drift down past the thicket and out of the frame, most of them never to land. The motion is slow and continuous, without drama: pressure applied evenly, everywhere, all the time.",
